  "scenario": "offshore-wind",
  "description": "600 MW of offshore wind on a Baltic hex two steps off Nadmorze (01 §5.2, 02 §8.1 in 0.22): 2.5x CAPEX for the site, 2 game days to build, and an HV spur ashore because 600 MW does not fit an MV line (500 MW). Days 0-1: the corridor Modrzyca - Turow - Nadmorze goes up and the start CCGT alone carries all three cities to a 310 MW evening peak. Day 2: the farm stands but its spur is still being laid, so everything it makes is curtailed for free (02 §5.1) - and the curtailed figure already flickers 600 - 200 - 0 - 400 - 600 as the gusts of the storm month cross the 25 m/s cutout inside single blocks (06 §6.3). Day 3: the spur goes live into the worst of it and 600 MW reads zero for the whole day; the gas plant carries the north alone, which is what it is for. Days 4-5: the sea comes back near rated power, the plant sits at zero for two days and 300-440 MW per turn is curtailed - the MV corridor south caps what the north can pass on. Money still falls over the six days: an offshore farm pays back in years, not in a week. The run is 06 §12.14 played out - offshore is base energy, not firm capacity.",
